!script {{
  --/| ==========================================================================
  --/| Tutorial 04: Reading D&D 2024 Beacon Repeating Rows
  --/|
  --/| PURPOSE
  --/| Many parts of a D&D character sheet are lists: actions, spells, items,
  --/| traits, resources, and so on. ScriptCards calls these repeating sections.
  --/| Each entry in one of those lists is a repeating row.
  --/|
  --/| This tutorial walks through the NPC Actions section one row at a time.
  --/|
  --/| HOW TO USE IT
  --/| 1. Select a D&D 2024 Beacon NPC that has at least one Action.
  --/| 2. Run this ScriptCard.
  --/| 3. The card will list the Action rows in the order ScriptCards reads them.
  --/| 4. The Mod console will also receive one Rdump of the first Action row.
  --/|
  --/| WHAT THIS TEACHES
  --/| rowcount tells us how many rows are in a repeating section.
  --/| Rfirst loads the first row.
  --/| [*R:name] reads the name from the row that is currently loaded.
  --/| [*R:$fieldlist$] lists the fields available on the loaded row.
  --/| Rdump prints the loaded row's fields to the Mod console for inspection.
  --/| Rnext moves to the next row.
  --/|
  --/| When there are no more rows, the repeating row is unloaded and a read
  --/| returns NoRepeatingAttributeLoaded.
  --/|
  --/| The special xxxActionIDxxxx value is the row ID ScriptCards uses for
  --/| repeating-row commands. Save it when you need to return to one particular
  --/| row later.
  --/|
  --/| CLASSIC REPEATING ROWS VS BEACON REPEATING ROWS
  --/| On older Roll20 sheets, repeating sections are built from traditional
  --/| Roll20 Attribute objects whose names begin with repeating_.
  --/|
  --/| Beacon stores the same kinds of information as native records instead.
  --/| With beaconsheet enabled, ScriptCards builds a compatible repeating-row
  --/| view from those Beacon records.
  --/|
  --/| This tutorial only reads information. It does not change the character.
  --/| ==========================================================================

  --#beaconsheet|1
  --#sourcetoken|@{selected|token_id}
  --&CharacterID|[*S:character_id]
  --#title|[*S:npc_name] - Repeating Rows Tutorial

  --+|[c][b]Repeating Section Overview[/b][/c]

  --&ActionCount|[*R:[&CharacterID]:repeating_npcaction:rowcount]
  --+Section|repeating_npcaction
  --+Number of Rows|[&ActionCount]

  --?"[&ActionCount]" -eq "0"|NoRows

  --+|[c][b]Inspect the First Row[/b][/c]

  --Rfirst|[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction

  --/| fieldlist is useful when you do not yet know which fields a row exposes.
  --+First Action|[*R:name]
  --+Available Fields|[*R:$fieldlist$]

  --/| Rdump writes the current row to the Mod console. It does not change which
  --/| row is loaded, so the script can continue reading the same row afterward.
  --Rdump|

  --+|[c][b]Read Every Action Row[/b][/c]

  --/| The first row is already loaded from the section above.
  --:ReadActionRow|

  --&ActionName|[*R:name]
  --?"[&ActionName]" -eq "NoRepeatingAttributeLoaded"|Finished

  --+|[b][&ActionName][/b]
  --+Description|[*R:description]
  --+Row ID|[*R:xxxActionIDxxxx]

  --Rnext|
  --^ReadActionRow|

  --:Finished|
  --+|[c][b]Finished[/b][/c]
  --+Result|All repeating_npcaction rows have been read.
  --X|

  --:NoRows|
  --+|[c][b]No Action Rows Found[/b][/c]
  --+Result|Select an NPC with at least one normal Action and run the tutorial again.
}}
